  "name": "Maplin-Sands-Trial27",
  "citation": "Puttock, J.S., Blackmore, D.R., Colenbrander, G.W. (1982). Field experiments on dense gas dispersion. J. Hazardous Materials 6, 13-41. Maplin Sands Trial 27. Arc-max concentrations digitised from Gant et al. (2016) Harmo17 Fig. 3.",
  "dataConfidence": "High",
  "description": "Maplin Sands Trial 27 - LNG spill on water from spill pipe. 23.2 kg/s for 160 s onto seawater (no impoundment). Sensors on floating pontoons at ~1 m above water on arcs at 90, 180, 325, 400, 525, 650 m. PHMSA MVD Rev B 2024 Table 2-35 base case. Sensor values digitised from Gant et al. 2016 Fig. 3 (Harmo17 paper) - confidence medium. Refine against original Puttock 1982 tables (PHMSA MVD spreadsheet) when available. DATA UPDATE: sensor values replaced by the PHMSA LNG Model Validation Database maximum arc-wise concentrations (3 s averaging, sensors 0.9 m above the water) as tabulated in DNV, 'LNG Validation for UDM 6.6', report to PHMSA (Oct 2010), Table 9: 89 m: 12.30 mol%, 131 m: 9.49 mol%, 324 m: 3.56 mol%, 400 m: 2.91 mol%, 650 m: 0.57 mol%. Mass fractions converted with CH4/air molar masses.",
